[quote]Three existed before all things. Their names were never ours to know.[/quote]
[h2]Overview[/h2]
[p]At the beginning of all things, there were three primordial entities. They are simply referred to as [b]A[/b], [b]B[/b], and [b]C[/b] - the Originals. Their true names were never known to mortals. Power was perfectly balanced between the three of them, and they co-existed in harmony.[/p]
[p]Together, they experimented with the power of creation that had been given to them: they created everything that exists: the outer planes, the inner planes, the material plane, and all the races and creatures that inhabit them.[/p]
[hr]
[h2]The Schism[/h2]
[p]Despite having created the mortal races together, [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] came to believe that creation was flawed. They wanted to destroy every mortal race and begin again from scratch - a clean slate. The accidental byproduct of [b]free will[/b] as a result of self-awareness, consciousness and rationality. This was unacceptable to [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] - they wanted beings who would worship without question.[/p]
[p][b]B[/b] disagreed. [b]B[/b] saw value in what they had made, respected the self-awareness, consciousness and rationality of the mortal races, and saw free will as the ultimate gift a creator could give to its creation, and refused to consent to annihilation. However, being alone against its two equally-powerful brethren, [b]B[/b] was outnumbered and could not prevent [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] from enacting their will through force.[/p]
[hr]
[h2]The Sacrifice[/h2]
[p]Unable to stop [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] through direct confrontation, [b]B chose a different path[/b]. [b]B[/b] sacrificed itself - shattering its own form and scattering its body, essence, and power across all of creation. This act is chronicled as @[The Great Sacrifice](myth:4433d5c7-1415-4837-afae-3d47c20f8f45). It suffused the cosmos with arcane energy, gave rise to @[The Arcane Weave](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_arcane_weave), and seeded the material plane with precious metals and gemstones. Over millennia, trace amounts of B's essence also condensed into the @[Arcane-Reactive Crystals](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_arcane_reactive_crystals) in the Material Plane, and B's scattered essence suffused nature itself and all living beings, laying the foundation of @[Primal & Nature Magic](Article:PLACEHOLDER_primal_nature_magic).[/p]
[p]With [b]B[/b]'s sacrifice, mortals were given the means to defend themselves. [b]B[/b] did not sacrifice to counter a specific plan - the invasion had not yet been conceived - but to give mortals a [b]general fighting chance[/b] to survive and resist whatever [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] would attempt.[/p]
[hr]
[h2]The Protective Shield[/h2]
[p]As a safety net, [b]B[/b]'s sacrifice also raised a protective effect across all planes of existence, lasting 100 years - see @[The Protective Shield](law:074714f8-5a2f-4737-8bc3-13822c1d8182). Its weakening eventually allowed the gods to open the planar rifts and unleash @[The Abominable End](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_abominable_end).[/p]
[hr]
[h2]Aftermath - The Plan Enacted[/h2]
[p]After [b]B[/b]'s sacrifice, [b]A and C subdivided themselves[/b] into lesser celestial beings - what would later be known as the gods. See @[The Gods and the Deception](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_gods_and_the_deception). This was a strategic choice: by becoming many, they could better manage, monitor, manipulate, harvest faith and divide the mortal races - who now possessed the gift of magic - against each other.[/p]
[p]True to their original intent, [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b]'s scattered fragments (the gods) ultimately enacted the genocide they had always wanted. They struck a pact with the powers of the [b]Abyss, Nine Hells, Shadowfell, and Feywild[/b], opened planar breaches along the coast of @[Kythoria](Article:PLACEHOLDER_kythoria), and unleashed the monster invasion upon the mortal races - an event that would come to be known as @[The Abominable End](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_abominable_end).[/p]
[hr]
[h2]The Hidden Truth[/h2]
[p]The gods actively hide the truth about the Originals. Mortals do not know that their deities were once part of two primordial entities, nor do they know that [b]B[/b] sacrificed itself to give them magic. This truth, if discovered, could turn the mortal races against the Gods and could eventually cause their deaths - something all Gods are secretly terrified of, and will refuse to enact the genocide directly unless victory is absolutely assured, without any casualty whatsoever - absolutely guaranteed.[/p]